node_modules/
dist/
build/
target/

# macOS filesystem sidecars. On a non-HFS volume (external exFAT drive,
# network share, container bind mount) macOS writes a `._<name>` resource
# fork beside every real file. This is not cosmetic here: a sidecar keeps
# the original extension, so several tools treat it as a real file and fail.
# Observed in this repository, all fixed at the source but worth listing:
#
#   * `aexeo-cli quality` aborted with "stream did not contain valid UTF-8"
#     because its source scan read every `*.rs` it found. A single `._lib.rs`
#     sidecar killed the whole gate. See quality/rust.rs
#     `is_unreadable_as_rust_source`.
#   * `vitest` collected `._plugin-host.test.ts` as a second copy of the real
#     suite, booting a competing workerd instance. See the plugin's
#     vitest.config.ts `exclude`.
#   * `llvm-profdata merge` failed outright on `._*.profraw` files, so
#     `cargo llvm-cov` could not produce a report at all.

# Aexeo audit artifacts. Only the current post-rename directory name is
# listed; the name used before the rename is intentionally absent because
# nothing writes it anymore.
.aexeo-reports/

# Local research scratch — paper PDFs and HTML downloads. Always
# session-local, never committed.
tmp/

# See the longer note near the top of this file: these sidecars have broken
# the quality gate, the plugin test runner, and coverage reporting, because
# they keep the extension of the file they shadow.
.DS_Store
._*

# Tooling scratch directories. These are local agent/tooling state, not
# part of the project, and must never be committed.
.aethyme/*
!.aethyme/config.toml
.chau7/

# Python leftovers from before the workspace moved to Rust. The last two
# Python artifacts in the repo (`.coveragerc`, `MANIFEST.in`) have been
# deleted. These patterns stay ignored so a stray local Python experiment
# cannot be committed by accident; nothing in this repository is Python.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

